WEBVTT

00:00:00.276 --> 00:00:03.873
<v><b>Emma Barnett:</b></v> Now, let’s meet and hear from Anthony Ray Hinton.

00:00:04.183 --> 00:00:09.084
He spent 28 years on death row for a double murder he didn’t commit.

00:00:09.377 --> 00:00:10.800
Anthony had an alibi,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.419
but that didn’t matter because he was black in Alabama.

00:00:14.649 --> 00:00:17.408
The police officers that arrested him were white,

00:00:17.511 --> 00:00:19.773
and the prosecutor who tried him was white,

00:00:19.948 --> 00:00:22.170
the jury that convicted him were white,

00:00:22.273 --> 00:00:25.044
and the judge who sentenced him was white.

00:00:25.643 --> 00:00:29.739
Ray got out of jail in 2015 when his conviction was quashed,

00:00:29.984 --> 00:00:35.015
and he is an extraordinary man – I spoke to him last week –

00:00:35.166 --> 00:00:40.618
warm, funny, and kind, not angry or bitter, as you might expect.